          "question": "How much difference does it make to how breathless I get?",
          "answer": "Stopping smoking can significantly impact your breathlessness. While it's the only intervention shown to slow the decline of lung function in people with COPD, directly addressing breathlessness also involves other approaches (guideline-copd-diagnosis-and-stepwise-management).\n\nBreathlessness during activity can lead to a cycle where you avoid activity, your muscles decondition, and then you experience breathlessness even sooner with less effort. Much of the improvement in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease comes from breaking this cycle through exercise and activity (lifestyle-copd-activity). Pulmonary rehabilitation, for example, is more effective at improving breathlessness and exercise capacity than inhalers alone (guideline-copd-diagnosis-and-stepwise-management).\n\nTherefore, stopping smoking helps to preserve your lung function over time, and engaging in activity and rehabilitation can directly improve how breathless you feel and your capacity for exercise.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.\n[sources: guideline-copd-diagnosis-and-stepwise-management, lifestyle-copd-activity]",
